      "css": ":host{--brand:#9d202e;--brand-hover:#7c1823;--brand-tint:oklch(95.5% 0.018 18);--brand-tint-2:oklch(90.5% 0.042 18);--desk:oklch(93.5% 0.006 75);--desk-deep:oklch(90% 0.008 75);--panel:oklch(98.6% 0.003 75);--paper:#fff;--ink:oklch(21% 0.006 30);--ink-2:oklch(38% 0.008 30);--ink-3:oklch(48% 0.008 30);--rule:oklch(87.5% 0.007 75);--rule-soft:oklch(92% 0.005 75);--up:oklch(45% 0.11 150);--danger:oklch(50% 0.17 27);--danger-tint:oklch(95.5% 0.03 27);--r-s:6px;--r-m:8px;--ease:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Hanken Grotesk','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink);} .ds-item{display:grid;grid-template-columns:22px 1fr auto;gap:4px 10px;align-items:center;width:300px;padding:9px 8px;border:0;border-radius:var(--r-s);background:none;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit;accent-color:var(--brand);} .ds-item:hover{background:var(--desk);} .ds-item:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brand);outline-offset:2px;} .ds-item[aria-current=true]{background:var(--brand-tint);} .ds-who b{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink);} .ds-item[aria-current=true] .ds-who b{color:var(--brand);} .ds-who span{display:block;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-3);} .ds-amt{text-align:right;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);} .ds-amt span{display:block;font-size:12px;color:var(--up);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Letter Sheet (excerpt)",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "letter-sheet",
      "description": "The signature object: paper with a layered shadow, bordeaux letterhead, left-aligned body, bordeaux fee-table header, superscript ordinals, bordeaux-tint field highlight.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sheet\"><div class=\"ds-lh\">ALTHO EXPERTISE</div><p class=\"ds-obj\">Objet : révision de nos honoraires au 1<sup>er</sup> janvier 2027</p><p>Nous tenons tout d'abord à vous remercier pour la confiance que vous accordez à <span class=\"ds-hl\">ALTHO EXPERTISE</span>.</p><table><tr><th>Mission</th><th>Actuel HT</th><th>Nouveau HT</th></tr><tr><td>Mission comptable</td><td>3 600 €</td><td>3 726 €</td></tr><tr class=\"ds-tot\"><td>Total annuel HT</td><td>6 240 €</td><td>6 456 €</td></tr></table></div>",
      "css": ":host{--brand:#9d202e;--brand-hover:#7c1823;--brand-tint:oklch(95.5% 0.018 18);--brand-tint-2:oklch(90.5% 0.042 18);--desk:oklch(93.5% 0.006 75);--desk-deep:oklch(90% 0.008 75);--panel:oklch(98.6% 0.003 75);--paper:#fff;--ink:oklch(21% 0.006 30);--ink-2:oklch(38% 0.008 30);--ink-3:oklch(48% 0.008 30);--rule:oklch(87.5% 0.007 75);--rule-soft:oklch(92% 0.005 75);--up:oklch(45% 0.11 150);--danger:oklch(50% 0.17 27);--danger-tint:oklch(95.5% 0.03 27);--r-s:6px;--r-m:8px;--ease:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Hanken Grotesk','Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink);} .ds-sheet{width:420px;padding:28px 36px;background:#fff;color:#1a1a1a;font:400 13px/1.34 'Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;box-shadow:0 1px 2px oklch(28% 0.01 30 / 0.10),0 8px 24px oklch(28% 0.01 30 / 0.10),0 24px 60px oklch(28% 0.01 30 / 0.08);} .ds-lh{font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',Arial,sans-serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;color:#9d202e;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:2px solid #9d202e;margin-bottom:16px;} .ds-sheet p{margin:0 0 8px;text-align:left;} .ds-obj{font-weight:700;} .ds-sheet sup{font-size:.66em;line-height:0;vertical-align:.5em;} .ds-hl{border-radius:3px;background:oklch(92% 0.04 18);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px oklch(92% 0.04 18);} .ds-sheet table{font-family:'Hanken Grotesk',Arial,sans-serif;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;} .ds-sheet th{background:#9d202e;color:#fff;font-weight:600;text-align:right;padding:4px 6px;} .ds-sheet th:first-child,.ds-sheet td:first-child{text-align:left;} .ds-sheet td{padding:3px 6px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #e3dcdc;} .ds-tot td{font-weight:700;background:#f6ebec;border-top:1px solid #9d202e;border-bottom:1px solid #9d202e;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Letter on the Desk",
    "overview": "The printed letter is the product. A white A4 sheet at true scale lies at the centre of a warm-grey daylight desk, with a real paper shadow under it, and every control around it (the client list on the left, the client record on the right, the settings form) exists to change what is on that paper. The interface is quiet so the sheet can be the loudest object on screen. There are no dashboard cards, no metric tiles and no spreadsheet chrome in the working view. The Clients view is a table because editing thirty rows of fees is table work, but it still sits on the same desk as a single bordered sheet.\n\nThe world is lit like an office in daylight. It has one ink: the bordeaux of the ALTHO letterhead. That bordeaux carries the primary action, the selection, the focus ring and the letter's own letterhead and table header. Everything else is warm-grey paper, hairline rules and near-black ink. Density is that of a working tool used once a year by a non-technical accountant. Labels are explicit French words, targets are 30 to 36px tall, and every amount uses tabular figures so columns of euros line up.\n\nType follows the Anthropic pairing the user asked for (a geometric grotesque over a text serif), set with free look-alikes embedded in the file: Hanken Grotesk for the interface and the letter's structure (letterhead, references, fee table, footer), Source Serif 4 for the letter's prose and address. The fonts print the same on every machine. The theme is light only. The office-daylight scene is the world, and a dark mode would turn the paper metaphor upside down.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A real-scale A4 sheet with a layered paper shadow is the centrepiece; panels frame it rather than compete with it.",
      "One accent ink (bordeaux #9d202e); all tints are bordeaux tints, never a second hue.",
      "Two families, one pairing: Hanken Grotesk (UI and letter structure) and Source Serif 4 (letter prose); tabular numerals everywhere.",
      "Hairline rules (1px) and 6–8px radii instead of cards and heavy borders.",
      "Flat panels; shadows are reserved for paper and for floating layers.",
      "Light theme only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Bordeaux is the only accent. Emphasis, selection, focus and the letter-to-field highlight are all bordeaux or bordeaux tints. There is no second highlight hue. Green, amber and red are status signals, not accents.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Desk Is Warm, the Ink Is Cool Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces sit at hue 75 (warm grey) and inks sit at hue 30 (a near-black with the faintest warmth). Don't introduce neutrals outside these two hues.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Pairing Rule",
        "body": "Hanken Grotesk and Source Serif 4, both embedded, are the only families. The serif is reserved for the letter's prose and address; the UI never uses it. Don't add a third face, and never ship Anthropic's licensed fonts (Styrene, Tiempos) in the file. Don't rely on a web font request; the file works offline.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` is set on the root and on the sheet. Every amount, percentage and count uses tabular figures, and amounts are right-aligned in every table and number input.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ragged-Right Letter Rule",
        "body": "Letter paragraphs are left-aligned, never justified. Justifying a 170mm measure at 10pt produced loose word spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Superscript Ordinal Rule",
        "body": "On the letter, \"1er\" is always set as `1<sup>er</sup>` (0.66em, raised 0.5em, zero line-height so line spacing is not disturbed).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Paper Casts a Shadow Rule",
        "body": "On the working surface, only the letter has a real shadow. Panels, lists and tables stay flat. If something needs separating, use a rule or a tone step.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the A4 sheet at the centre of any view that edits letter content, and let the controls around it change it live.",
      "Do use bordeaux (#9d202e) as the single accent for the primary action, selection and focus, and bordeaux tints for every highlight, including the letter-to-field link.",
      "Do set every amount in tabular figures and right-align it.",
      "Do keep letter paragraphs left-aligned and set \"1er\" as a superscript ordinal.",
      "Do show placeholder text only on the on-screen letter and make sure the print render never contains it.",
      "Do separate panels with 1px rules and the panel/desk tone step; keep radii at 6px for controls and 8px for floating layers and tables.",
      "Do embed Hanken Grotesk and Source Serif 4 in the file so the app and the letter render identically offline."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce a second accent hue. Amber, green and red are status signals only, and the field highlight is bordeaux, not yellow.",
      "Don't justify letter text.",
      "Don't add a second type family or a system display face.",
      "Don't add a dark theme; the world is an office in daylight.",
      "Don't wrap content in shadowed cards or build admin-dashboard metric tiles; only the paper and floating layers cast shadows.",
      "Don't let the envelope window, highlights, placeholders or the paper shadow reach the printed page."
    ]
  }
}
